  data:  # 220e
    kind: work_item  # 220e
    title: "_module_matches arm 3 accepts a hint with MORE leading components than the row (mycsvlib.csv -> stdlib csv, koel's @/services/http -> node http); go's under-qualified filepath/grpc rows depend on it"  # 220e
    status: todo_hard  # 220e
    priority: 2  # 220e
    parent:  # 220e
    tags:  # 220e
    - analysis_quality  # 220e
    - adr_0017  # 220e
    isbefore: []  # 220e
    duplicate_of: []  # 220e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 220e
    pr_ref:  # 220e
    description: "FOUND BY WI-nibav (2026-10-01), which had to decide whether defusedcsv should be identified by a catalogue row or by _module_matches' component-suffix arm.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. io_boundary._module_matches arm 3 (\"dropped qualification\") accepts a match when one side's components are a SUFFIX of the other's, in EITHER direction. Its docstring justifies only one direction: the EDGE HINT is the unqualified tail of the catalogue's qualified module (go `http` for `net/http`, java `System` for `java.lang.System`). The other direction -- the hint carries LEADING components the catalogue row does not -- is a more-qualified owner path, which under ADR-0051's axiom is normally a DIFFERENT owner: `mycsvlib.csv.writer` classifies as stdlib `csv.writer` (fs_write) today, verified on real analyzer output.\n\nMEASURED, not argued. In-process A/B over 29 existing baseline surveys (python pretix; go argo-cd; c crun/passt/haproxy/redis/torsocks/tmate; objc AFNetworking/CocoaLumberjack/SDWebImage/fmdb/ReactiveObjC/ResearchKit; swift vapor/Alamofire; elixir phoenix/plausible/livebook; php+ts koel; js sharp/nuclear; ts nest; java confluent/jenkins; scala lila; cpp powerdns/sherpa-onnx). Arm A = shipped matcher; arm B = the same, refusing a match decided ONLY by the hint-longer suffix arm (controls asserted in the instrument: csv<-defusedcsv.csv refused; java.lang.System<-System, os/exec<-os.exec.Cmd, net/http<-http, csv<-csv kept). Tagging is the shipped tag_io_boundaries on the shipped rehydration, default community overlays loaded. Result: 4 repos move, 4 (catalogue, hint) pairs, 78 tagged edges:\n- go argo-cd, 24 edges, TRUE positives: catalogue `filepath` <- hint `path/filepath` (Walk 16, WalkDir 3, Glob 1) and overlay `grpc` <- `google.golang.org/grpc` (NewClient 4). They match only because go.yaml:66 spells the module `filepath` and go-x-sys-and-grpc.yaml:75 spells it `grpc` -- UNDER-QUALIFIED rows (ADR-0051 says the key is the import path).\n- c powerdns, 9 edges: catalogue `time` <- `sys/time` (from `sys/time.h`). `time()` is declared in <time.h>/<ctime>, not <sys/time.h>; these classify only because `ctime` is not folded to `time` (io_boundary._HEADER_SUFFIXES comment refuses the c-prefix strip). True by luck.\n- php/ts koel, 41 edges, FALSE positives: javascript catalogue `http` <- hint `@/services/http`, koel's OWN tsconfig path alias. `http.get` from a first-party module tagged net_send as node's http.\n- python pretix, 4 edges: `csv` <- `defusedcsv.csv`. WI-nibav gave defusedcsv its own community row, so this pair no longer decides any classification (prefer_exact_owner picks the row).\nEvery other survey: 0 diffs. NOT covered: rust, kotlin, haskell, ruby, erlang, go beyond argo-cd, python beyond pretix.\n\nWHY WI-nibav DID NOT CHANGE THE PREDICATE. Refusing the direction outright loses the 24 go true positives and the 9 c ones to remove 41 false ones. And a second consumer DEPENDS on the hint-longer direction: taint's resolved-edge gate (taint.py, WI-damir) compares a catalogue module against a module derived from a FILE PATH (`hypergumbo_core.cli` vs `packages.….hypergumbo_core.cli`), where leading components are directories, not owner identity.\n\nPROPOSED ORDER, not decided: (1) qualify the under-qualified rows (go filepath -> path/filepath; overlay grpc -> google.golang.org/grpc; decide c's <ctime> spelling) so they match by arm 1/2; (2) then refuse the hint-longer suffix in the MODULE-SLOT filter (named_lookup_arm) only, keeping it for the path-derived taint gate; (3) re-run this A/B and require go/c diffs to be 0 and the koel shape to drop. Instrument and per-repo outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/nibav/measure_suffix.py and measure/*.json."  # 220e
    fields: {}  # 220e
