  message: "SECOND PASS, 15 more surveys made fresh on WI-nibav's tree (gin, coredns, alertmanager, ripgrep, hadolint, servant, postal, spring-petclinic, okhttp, fastapi, robyn, cowboy, http4s, howler.js, detekt), same instrument. Two more repos move, both go, both the same under-qualified rows: coredns 10 edges (filepath<-path/filepath Walk 6, grpc<-google.golang.org/grpc NewClient 4), alertmanager 1 (filepath.Glob). Zero diffs in rust, haskell (hadolint, servant), ruby (postal), java (spring-petclinic), kotlin (okhttp, detekt), python (fastapi, robyn), erlang (cowboy), scala (http4s), js (howler.js).\nTOTAL over 44 surveys: 6 repos, 89 tagged edges decided only by the hint-longer direction: go 35 true positives (argo-cd 24, coredns 10, alertmanager 1), c 9 true-by-luck (powerdns sys/time->time), ts 41 false positives (koel @/services/http), python 4 (pretix defusedcsv, now absorbed by its own row). What this does NOT show: any adjudication beyond reading the primitive and the hint; behaviour on repos outside these 44; taint verdict movement (the A/B was io tagging only)."  # 0d43
- op: discuss  # 30a4
  at: '2026-10-03T06:41:58Z'  # 30a4
  by: agent  # 30a4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 30a4
  clock: 3  # 30a4
  nonce: 30a4  # 30a4
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; scope gap added.\n- Arm 3 is still bidirectional (io_boundary.py ~4930). _module_matches is True for csv<-mycsvlib.csv, http<-@/services/http, filepath<-path/filepath, grpc<-google.golang.org/grpc, time<-sys/time. lookup_with_module('get','@/services/http') gives http.get net_send in both the JS and TS catalogues.\n- KOEL STILL REPRODUCES at HEAD: koel's real tsconfig.json + http.ts + authService.ts + encyclopediaService.ts. The survey emits module_attr_ref -> typescript:@/services/http:0-0:@/services/http.get, and measure_suffix.py gives A=4 B=1 diffs=3, all net_send http.get. WI-fukaf (#1231) did not remove it.\n- MISSED DEPENDENT ROWS: besides go.yaml:66 filepath and go-x-sys-and-grpc.yaml:75 grpc, the golang.org/x/sys/unix rows go-x-sys-and-grpc.yaml:50/55/60 (module unix) match only through arm 3; the io_boundary.py ~1337 docstring cites this pairing. Put them in step (1) beside filepath/grpc. (The 44-survey A/B probably had no x/sys/unix user; inference, not measured.)\n- Second consumer still depends on it: taint.py ~1261-1268 calls _module_matches against a path-derived module.\n- No item covers koel's @/ alias or mycsvlib; WI-nibav (done) absorbed only pretix/defusedcsv via its own row.\n- NOT CHECKED: rust/kotlin/haskell/ruby catalogues for other under-qualified rows."  # 30a4
